# Test: a DHCP server the reload removes leaves show system dns.
# Initial config: the observer plugin and service dhcp-server on link
#   zedhwdr, one subnet 198.18.21.0/24 whose dns-source names configured,
#   with dns-server 198.51.100.1.
# After SIGHUP: the observer plugin alone; the service block is gone, so the
#   engine removes the dhcpserver plugin while the daemon runs.
# Expected: show system dns lists the dhcpserver selection at
#   "service dhcp-server shared-network subnet dns-source", instance
#   198.18.21.0/24, before the reload, and after it still answers the
#   router's selection (consumer system) but no dhcpserver consumer at all.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-home-cpe-23b review round 3 ISSUE 3: the DHCP server's
#   OnBye handler (internal/plugins/dhcpserver/register.go) sends its
#   withdrawal while the engine removes the plugin, inside the removal
#   grace, and the registry forgets the consumer. The dhcpserver unit test
#   in publish_test.go calls withdraw() directly, so it proves
#   neither the wiring nor that the emit is read during removal.
# PREVENTS: a removed DHCP server whose last selections show system dns and
#   ze doctor keep reporting until the daemon restarts.
#
# DISCRIMINATION: break overlay rwinv/c23b-withdraw-dhcp/ (publisher.withdraw()
#   taken out of the OnBye handler): the registry keeps a dhcpserver
#   consumer, with an empty selection list, after the reload removed the
#   plugin. Observed red (rwinv/out-gb15/b15-withdraw-dhcp.log:46): "the
#   removed dhcpserver is still listed with 0 selection(s)". The poll also
#   requires the system consumer's "system dns-source" selection, which
#   proves the answer it judged came from a live registry, not an empty one.
#
# Sequencing: dhcp/link creates the link before ze starts, because the
#   server publishes a subnet only once it listens there. The observer
#   writes observer.initial-ok once the subnet is listed; the trigger waits
#   for it, copies config2.conf over ze-bgp.conf, sends SIGHUP and writes
#   reload.done, after which the observer polls for the withdrawal.
#
# No cmd= line carries `:timeout=` on ze: a foreground command's timeout
# replaces option=timeout as the budget of the whole test.

option=needs-linux:caps=net-admin,net-raw
option=timeout:value=60s

stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
plugin {
	external show-system-dns-withdraw-dhcp-test {
		run "le test fixture plugin/show-system-dns-withdraw-dhcp"
		encoder json
	}
}
service {
	dhcp-server {
		enabled true
		listen-interface zedhwdr
		shared-network home {
			subnet 198.18.21.0/24 {
				range household {
					start 198.18.21.100
					stop 198.18.21.110
				}
				lease-time 3600
				dns-server 198.51.100.1
				dns-source {
					source configured
				}
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

tmpfs=config2.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF2
plugin {
	external show-system-dns-withdraw-dhcp-test {
		run "le test fixture plugin/show-system-dns-withdraw-dhcp"
		encoder json
	}
}
EOF_CONF2

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test fixture dhcp/link zedhwdr 198.18.21.7/24:exit=0
cmd=background:seq=2:exec=le test fixture plugin/show-system-dns-withdraw-trigger
cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=OK: show system dns lists the DHCP server's subnet selection before the reload
expect=stderr:contains=OK: show system dns drops the removed DHCP server and keeps the router selection
reject=stderr:contains=reload error
reject=stderr:pattern=panic
